---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SavingsGoalLab from "../../components/SavingsGoalLab.tsx";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Savings Goal Planner"
  description="Put a number and a date on a savings goal — a down payment, a car, a wedding — and find the monthly amount that gets you there, with investment growth doing part of the work."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Personal Finance · Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Savings goal planner</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A goal without a monthly number is just a wish. Set the target and the date,
      and this works backward to the amount you'd need to set aside each month —
      letting whatever return you earn along the way carry part of the load.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <SavingsGoalLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Matching the goal to the account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Near-term goals belong in safe cash.</strong> If you need the money
          in a year or two — a car, a wedding, a house down payment — keep it in a
          high-yield savings account or money-market fund. A market drop right before
          you need it can blow up the plan, and there isn't time to recover.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Distant goals can take more risk.</strong> The further off the goal,
          the more of the work investment returns can do — and the more short-term
          volatility you can ride out. That's the difference between saving for next
          year and investing for a decade out.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Time is the cheapest lever.</strong> Stretching the deadline drops
          the monthly number twice over: fewer months to cover the same goal, and more
          time for growth to compound. Starting earlier beats saving harder.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Automate the transfer for the day after payday, and the goal funds itself
        quietly in the background. Educational only, not advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pf-related">
    <h2 class="pf-related-heading">Keep exploring</h2>
    <ul class="grid grid--2 pf-related-grid">
      <li>
        <a href="/personal-finance/budget" class="card">
          <h3>Free up the monthly amount</h3>
          <p>The 50/30/20 budget helps you find room for a goal like this in your take-home pay.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/tools/compound-growth" class="card">
          <h3>For long-horizon goals</h3>
          <p>The Growth tool shows how much of a distant goal compounding can cover if you start early.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro { padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md); max-width: var(--measure-wide); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--color-text-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
  .wl-explainer { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
  .pf-related { margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
  .pf-related-heading { font-size: var(--step-1); padding-bottom: var(--space-xs); border-bottom: var(--border); margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }
  .pf-related-grid { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .pf-related-grid a.card { height: 100%; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; display: block; }
  .pf-related-grid h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .pf-related-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .ss-headline { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.15rem; padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--color-accent-soft); border: 1px solid var(--color-accent); }
  .ss-headline-label { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .ss-headline-value { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--step-3); line-height: 1.1; color: var(--color-accent); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .ss-headline-sub { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .ss-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-sm); margin: 0 0 var(--space-md); }
  .ss-stats > div { background: var(--color-surface-alt); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: var(--space-sm); }
  .ss-stats dt { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--color-muted); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  .ss-stats dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--step-0); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
</style>
